e":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.6 stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen I hide a node and then unhide it the camera centers on the given node.\n\nThis is incredible annoying when you need to compare couple nodes and such. The camera keeps jumping around.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add a 2D node, such as a Control, Node2d, ...\n2. Move it somewhere in the scene if you wish.\n3. Click on the eye icon in the scene tree to hide it and then immediately agian to unhide it (it does not need to be very fast like regular mouse double click, there's a pretty big delay in between the two clicks which results in the camera centering).\n4. Observe the camera now centered on your node you just showed.\n(5. Hide it again, then wait couple seconds, then unhide it, that's way the camera does not center, this is such an annoying workflow sorry but I can't describe it better than really annoying.)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNo need for any, just open the editor and add a Control/Node2d node.","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"http